  "term": "self-discipline",
  "definition": "In this historical psychology source, self-discipline means the deliberate training of one’s own habits through steady, repeated mental effort. It refers to practices like regularly reviewing and organizing experience so that attention and recall become more effective, even if basic retentiveness itself is not changed.",
